@*
    Task 13.1 — the ASP.NET Core replacement for this plugin's web.config
    <system.web.webPages.razor><pages> element (Requirement 4.4).

    PART OF THE PLUGIN RECIPE. See
    src/Plugins/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles/Views/_ViewImports.cshtml for the full
    reasoning. In brief: all 20 plugins ship a byte-identical web.config declaring
    pageBaseType="Nop.Web.Framework.ViewEngines.Razor.WebViewPage" (→ the @inherits below, which
    is what makes T("…") resolve and an unqualified @model resolve) plus four System.Web
    <namespaces> (→ the @using directives; System.Web.Mvc.Ajax has no ASP.NET Core counterpart and
    is dropped).

    It sits at Views/ and inside the project file's Content/Link glob (Views\**\*.cshtml), so this
    file and the four views link into the SAME directory
    (/Plugins/Pickup.PickupInStore/Views/) — Razor resolves imports by walking up from the view's
    LINKED path. Linking them inconsistently would make the imports silently not apply and the
    failure would look like a missing model type.

    NOTE Create.cshtml / Edit.cshtml / _CreateOrUpdate.cshtml all declare `@model` FULLY QUALIFIED
    (Nop.Plugin.Pickup.PickupInStore.Models.StorePickupPointModel), and Configure.cshtml declares
    no @model at all, so the @using of the plugin's own Models namespace is not strictly required
    here — it is included for consistency with the other plugins' _ViewImports.
*@
@inherits Nop.Web.Framework.ViewEngines.Razor.WebViewPage<TModel>

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Rendering
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing

@*
    Nop.Web.Framework carries HtmlExtensions (Html.NopLabelFor / NopEditorFor / NopTextAreaFor /
    NopDropDownListFor / FieldIdFor), ViewCompatibilityExtensions and ChildActionExtensions, plus
    Extensions.SelectionIsNotPossible (used by the store dropdown in _CreateOrUpdate). One import
    covers all of them.
*@
@using Nop.Core.Infrastructure
@using Nop.Web.Framework
@using Nop.Web.Framework.UI
@using Nop.Plugin.Pickup.PickupInStore.Models

@*
    Tag helpers. 3.90 had none (they do not exist in MVC 5). Added for the same reason task 7.3
    added them to Nop.Web: the framework's form/validation tag helpers are the supported route to
    an anti-forgery token, and Html.BeginForm uses the same infrastructure.
*@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
